<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-12">12 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">First long-distance radio message sent from the Eiffel Tower</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">A transmitter on the Eiffel Tower sent a wireless message over a record distance. The tower's value for military radio helped secure its future after its original 20-year permit.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-21">21 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">New York passes an ordinance banning women from smoking in public</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Sullivan Ordinance barred managers of public places from allowing women to smoke. Mayor George McClellan vetoed it two weeks later, but it reflected anxieties about women's changing roles.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/london" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/london.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-24">24 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Baden-Powell publishes 'Scouting for Boys'</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The first instalment of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/robert-baden-powell-1st-baron-baden-powell">Robert Baden-Powell</a>'s handbook on outdoor skills and citizenship appeared in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a>. Boys began forming patrols of their own, and the Scout movement spread worldwide.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/june-30">30 June</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Tunguska explosion flattens Siberian forest</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">An asteroid or comet fragment exploded above the Tunguska river, levelling some 2,000 square km of forest. It is the largest impact event in recorded history.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/july-26">26 July</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The Bureau of Investigation, forerunner of the FBI, is created</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Attorney General Charles Bonaparte set up a force of special agents in the US Justice <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">Department</a>. Renamed the FBI in 1935, it grew under J. Edgar Hoover into America's main federal police agency.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/september-16">16 September</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">William Durant incorporates General Motors</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Buick head William Durant formed General Motors as a holding company, soon adding Oldsmobile, Cadillac and others. GM became for decades the world's largest car maker.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/bitola" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bitola.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/november-22">22 November</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The Congress of Manastir standardises the Albanian alphabet</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">A national conference held in Manastir from 14 November closed, having set out to standardise the Albanian alphabet, until then written in six or more distinct alphabets. The day is kept as Alphabet Day in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albania">Albania</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kosovo">Kosovo</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-macedonia">North Macedonia</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bitola">Manastir</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/december-28">28 December</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">An earthquake and tsunami destroy Messina</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">A powerful earthquake and tsunami struck the Strait of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/messina">Messina</a>, destroying Messina in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reggio-calabria">Reggio Calabria</a>. Around 75,000 to 80,000 people died, making it <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>'s deadliest recorded earthquake.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a></div></div></li></ol></section>
