<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">In the profiles</h2><ul class="yr-prof"><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-ecuador"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Ecuador.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Ecuador</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Guayaquil–Quito railway reaches Quito</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/congo-free-state"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Congo%20Free%20State.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Congo Free State</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Belgium annexes the territory as the Belgian Congo</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/nahda"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Nahda.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Nahda</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Ottoman constitution is restored, loosening censorship, and the Egyptian University opens in Cairo</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/culture/hongshan-culture"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Hongshan%20culture.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Hongshan culture</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Japanese archaeologist Torii Ryūzō discovers the Hongshanhou site at Chifeng</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/young-turks"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Young%20Turks.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Young Turks</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Unionist officers of the Third Army mutiny and the sultan restores the constitution, opening the Second Constitutional Era</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/imperialism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Imperialism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Imperialism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">After scandal upon scandal over atrocities in the Congo Free State, Belgium is forced to take it over from King Leopold II</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/kemalism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kemalism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kemalism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Young Turk Revolution reinstates the Ottoman constitution; Atatürk is a member of the Committee of Union and Progress</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/angkor-wat"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Angkor%20Wat.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Angkor Wat</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The École française d'Extrême-Orient sets up the Conservation d'Angkor to clear and restore the temples</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/taj-mahal"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Taj%20Mahal.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Taj Mahal</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The restoration ordered by the viceroy Lord Curzon is completed</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/culture/vinca-culture"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Vin%C4%8Da%20culture.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Vinča culture</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Miloje Vasić discovered the type site, Vinča-Belo Brdo</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/medina"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Medina.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Medina</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Hejaz railway from Damascus reaches Medina</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/empress-dowager-cixi"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Empress%20Dowager%20Cixi.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Empress Dowager Cixi</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">She dies a day after the Guangxu Emperor, having chosen his nephew Puyi as successor</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/persian-constitutional-revolution"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Persian%20Constitutional%20Revolution.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Persian Constitutional Revolution</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Mohammad Ali Shah stages a coup and bombards the parliament, beginning the Minor Tyranny</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/mau-movement"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Mau%20movement.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Mau movement</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">A dispute between the German colonial administration and the Samoan Council of Chiefs over a native-owned copra business leads to the formation of the Mau a Pule on Savai'i</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/gandhism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Gandhism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Gandhism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Gandhi coins the word sarvodaya as the title of his translation of Ruskin's Unto This Last</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/religion/ahmadiyya"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Ahmadiyya.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Ahmadiyya</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Ahmad dies and Hakeem Noor-ud-Din is elected the first Caliph</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/religion/tenrikyo"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Tenrikyo.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Tenrikyo</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Tenrikyo is officially recognised as one of the thirteen branches of Sect Shinto</span></li></ul></section>
